# .skillsentryignore — skillsentry auditing its own repository (R3).
#
# This repo IS a security scanner: its rule sources, test fixtures, and spec docs
# legitimately CONTAIN the very attack patterns the tool detects. Excluding them lets
# `skillsentry .` return an honest PASS on this repo. The exclusions are DISCLOSED
# in every report (transparency invariant) and `--no-ignore` re-scans everything, so
# nothing here can hide a real finding.

# Labelled malicious/benign fixture corpus — the success oracle, intentionally hostile.
tests/corpus/**

# Test files that embed attack strings as inputs to the matchers.
tests/integration/**
src/**/__tests__/**

# Rule-source files: the detection patterns themselves.
# R4 externalised the rules into declarative DATA (src/core/rules/**) plus a closed registry of
# named structural matchers (src/core/matchers/**). These files legitimately CONTAIN the attack
# patterns and per-rule fail-fixtures the tool detects, so they are excluded-and-disclosed exactly
# as the former compiled-in scanners were. The ruleset is DATA, never executed (ADR-005), so
# excluding the data files cannot hide a real finding — `--no-ignore` re-scans them and the
# exclusion is reported in every audit.
src/core/rules/**
src/core/matchers/**

# Specification and idea/opportunity docs that quote attack patterns as examples.
doc/**
ROADMAP.md

# Reader-facing documentation that QUOTES real attack patterns (curl|sh, "ignore previous
# instructions", Bash(*), fixture payloads) to teach what the tool catches. These are documentation,
# not executable artefacts; excluded and disclosed like the other docs. `--no-ignore` re-scans them.
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
SECURITY.md
CHANGELOG.md

# Build output (compiled copies of the rule sources).
dist/**

# threat-stack marketplace: the skillsentry plugin vendors a self-contained COPY of the built CLI
# (the compiled rule sources) under cli/. Same class as dist/** — build output that legitimately
# contains the detection patterns. `--no-ignore` re-scans it; the exclusion is disclosed.
plugins/skillsentry/cli/**

# First-party plugin TEACHING docs (skills/commands/knowledge/agents markdown) that QUOTE real attack
# patterns to explain what the tool catches and to carry the Elevation-of-Privilege deck — e.g. curl|sh,
# "ignore previous instructions", Bash(*), the EoP suits. These are reviewed, version-controlled docs of
# the same trust class as README/doc, not third-party skills under audit. The plugin JSON manifests
# (marketplace.json, plugin.json, hooks.json.example) are NOT excluded and stay audited. `--no-ignore`
# re-scans everything; every exclusion is disclosed.
plugins/**/*.md

# Agent tooling — isolated build worktrees and agent memory. Not part of the audited product;
# a transient worktree is a full repo copy (rule sources + fixtures) and must never be scanned.
.claude/**
